// =============================================================================
// THT Dual Scan — Combined  ·  DEPRECATED
// =============================================================================
// This single-script approach is deprecated because Pine v6 cannot render a
// clean table.new() on the price pane from a non-overlay indicator. The
// force_overlay'd box+label workaround looks like garbage.
//
// Use TWO indicators instead — they share the same color palette and play
// together on a single chart:
//
//   1. THT Dual Scan — FVB         (overlay=true, on price pane)
//      → cloud, halo'd bands, basis with halo, BUY/SELL labels
//      → status table at top-right of price pane (native, clean)
//
//   2. THT Dual Scan — B-Xtrender  (overlay=false, in oscillator pane)
//      → histogram, halo'd smoothed lines, crossover diamonds
//
// Both files are in this repo. Open each in Pine Editor, Save, Add to chart.
// =============================================================================
//@version=6
indicator("THT Dual Scan — DEPRECATED, use FVB + BXT scripts", overlay = true)

// Show a notice on the chart so users know to switch
if barstate.islast
    label.new(bar_index, high, "DEPRECATED — use the two separate scripts:\nTHT Dual Scan — FVB\nTHT Dual Scan — B-Xtrender",
              style = label.style_label_down, color = #FFAA00, textcolor = color.black,
              size = size.normal, text_font_family = font.family_default)
